  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> Zener diode along with a series resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is connected across a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> supply (as shown in the figure). If the maximum Zener current is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math>, then the minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/21f9da59-2641-4db6-9b82-354f5b5df9cb-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 113px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "480",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the current through Zener diode and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;through load resistor.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ef504f92-3f59-4766-9a84-88bdc675e581-image.png\" style=\"width: 330px; height: 180px;\" />​​​​​​​</p><p>As maximum current flows through Zener diode, hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&there4;</mo></math>Maximum current,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mA</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p><p>Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;is voltage drop across Zener <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.&nbsp;<br />Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> is maximum, hence minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mi>I</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>480</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
